//
// A LIBRARY'S OWN FUNCTION BELOW ITS CALL WINS OVER THE STANDARD LIBRARY'S (`@FR-F-Surface`:
// L's own code reaches all of its items, in any order of its file; `@FR-Disp-Key`).  The
// fixture library beside this cell calls four functions it defines further down, each named
// like a standard-library function.  Pass 1 meets the call before the definition, and took
// the standard library's: `type_named(1, "abc")` was refused as "Too many parameters for
// type_named", the same-arity `chr(4) + 1` was typed as the stdlib's return (loft#2331).  A
// PROGRAM may not define a standard-library name at all; a library may, so the cell reaches
// the shape through one.
//
// Values hand-computed in the fixture: 4, 41, 7, 78, and the definition-first control 5.
//
// @falsified-at: 0e95172cd (loft#2331) — interpret and native-c: refused, "Too many parameters
//   for type_named" in the fixture.
// CHANNEL: the asserts, and the refusal on the broken build.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the message prints the answers.

use f_surface_2331_lib;

fn main() {
  s = "{f_surface_2331_lib::go_more()} {f_surface_2331_lib::go_same()} {f_surface_2331_lib::go_record()} {f_surface_2331_lib::go_loop()} {f_surface_2331_lib::go_first()}";
  assert(s == "4 41 7 78 5", "the library's own calls: {s}");
}
